@flexiarg pattern-interpretation/cite-the-source-bytes
@title Interpret From The Pattern's Own Bytes, Clause By Clause
@keywords interpretation, citation, source-binding, flexiarg, compile-clause, stand-in
@audience interpretation jobs, admission reviewers, cascade-model builders
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; implementation futon2 src/futon2/aif/interpretation_evidence.clj:176-193 validates the record; design PROPOSAL-pattern-interpretation D1 by claude-4, not yet approved)
@references [pattern-interpretation/declare-the-universe pattern-interpretation/compile-guards-exactly translation/bind-to-the-source hygiene/observe-the-authority]
@see-also contracts/resolve-pointers-at-head
@why an interpretation is only checkable against the text it claims to render. The live shadow G read patterns through a word-level compiler (cascade_model_manifest/compile-clause) — a stand-in for the pattern — which reads 93 of 1352 library patterns; 1714 IF/HOWEVER clauses come back :uninterpretable-guard and 145 are missing, so almost every real cascade refuses. Prediction and enactment also read the pattern through different readers, so they cannot share one transition model.
@how the interpretation record names the pattern and its source file by sha256; quotes the pattern's IF, HOWEVER and THEN verbatim, each cited to the source bytes; shows repository membership by quote; and is the only reading both prediction and enactment consume. An uncited clause, a clause from a different source, or a membership quote that does not contain the pattern id refuses (:citation-missing, :clause-source-mismatch, :repository-membership-invalid).
@violation-signature a guard with no clause quotes; a paraphrase in place of a quote; prediction reading prose while enactment reads the record; an interpretation that survives an edit to the pattern file because nothing pins its bytes.
! conclusion: Every interpretation quotes and cites the pattern's clauses to its sha-pinned bytes, and both prediction and enactment read that one record.

  + context: The War Machine scores and enacts cascades of library patterns written as prose flexiargs.

  + IF:
    A pattern must become executable guards and effects.

  + HOWEVER:
    A compiler over words is cheap and covers little; an agent's reading is broad but unverifiable unless tied to the text.

  + THEN:
    Bind each clause of the interpretation to quoted, sha-pinned source bytes and make that record the single reading.

  + BECAUSE:
    The quote is the one part of a translation that can be checked by identity; everything else is checked against it.

  + evidence: claude-4's shadow-G record WM-10-LIVE-SHADOW-G.md (93/1352; 1714 uninterpretable clauses); the M-zaif-harness-v1 interpreted record (futon2 holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/F13-model-manifest-2026-09-15/redo/interpreted-pattern-set.edn) as a real cited example.
